# Patch 0007 — skill: a tracked file is never written through Bash, and the comments folder goes in the commit
# Offered back: yes
# Files: skill/SKILL.md
#
# Reason: two gaps a host's dry run (2026-09-09) and its user (2026-09-10) found. First, the skill
# forbade the Edit/Write/MultiEdit tools on a tracked file and said nothing of the shell: an agent working
# in a mode that writes files through Bash (cp, tee, a heredoc, sed -i) ran track-config and cp in one
# compound command on a tracked file, and since track-config exits 0 when tracking is ON, the `&&` ran the
# copy on exactly the file it must not touch; the write landed raw with no suggestion recorded. The
# "When tracking is ON" section now opens with the rule: no shell write to a tracked file in any of its
# forms, every write through track-edit, and track-config's exit code checked as a step of its own, never
# in a compound command with the write. Second, agents never added `.trackchanges/` to their commits, so
# the reviewer's comments and the record of the agent's changes were not archived with the work; a Notes
# bullet asks the agent to include the folder when the project has one and does not ignore it (the
# store is designed to be committed: store-io.mjs's header). Prose only; pinned by the host's
# tools/vendor-patches.test.mjs (P7) and the drift test.
